{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-running-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.48: `rates-running`, the Rates-scale twin of `process-crankcase-running` with `chain-tog-speciation`'s hydrocarbons and running Total Energy -- THC, CO and NOx from running exhaust (1) and crankcase running (15), methane, NMHC, NMOG and TOG from running exhaust -- for the gasoline-selected passenger car in Washtenaw County on road types 1 and 4, at `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>`. MOVES's execution `runspecroadtype` holds all five road types, as it does for any run that selects road type 1 (conventions §102).\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. Three things `scale-rates` cannot: (1) CHAINED pollutants per speed bin -- crankcase from running, the hydrocarbon species two and three rungs deep -- which are the inventory's chain applied to the per-bin rate; (2) OFF-NETWORK IDLE at Rates scale, one RatePerDistance row per cohort at `avgSpeedBinID` 0 on link `(zoneID*10 + 1)*100`, whose value is a rate per idle HOUR of a vehicle of that fuel (the inventory's idle quantity over the cohort's idle hours: measured, its ratio to road type 1's SHO is the fuel's share); and (3) crankcase running on road type 1, which MOVES chains from off-network idle and the inventory had never been asked for.\n\nTHE BINDINGS. `n_ratesScale` = 1 and `n_outputRate` = 6125, the (pollutant-process, road type, cohort) pairs across five road types, checked by `rateSurvivorCount`.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "rates-running"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-running/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecmonth": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-running/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecmonth.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecmonth"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, monthID 8.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspechour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-running/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspechour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, hourID 7. Six in the RunSpec XML, seven here: the XML's @key is a 0-based index into the sorted hour list (docs/mixed-onroad.md 0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_aggregationhour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-running/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_aggregationhour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "The hours the run aggregates over. This run does not set `aggregateBy`, so it is `runspechour` itself and the same file.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-running/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, dayID 5 (weekday). The second factor of the activity axis and of the output axis, and its extent is one in this run: `<day id=\"5\">` selects one day type where the earlier `<day key=\"5\">` was an out-of-range INDEX and fell back to both (moves.rs PR #55).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_rateday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-running/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_rateday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "The day types the RATE-side time pre-aggregation is scoped to. This run does not set `aggregateBy`, so it is `runspecday` itself and the same file: the pre-aggregation averages over one cell and returns the table's own value. A run that aggregates points this somewhere else, because MOVES overwrites `runspecday` with the synthesized output day AFTER the pre-aggregation has run.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_actday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-running/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_actday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "The day types the output day's ACTIVITY covers. This run does not set `aggregateBy`, so it is `runspecday` itself and the same file, and `noOfRealDays` is that one day type's.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
